I am having some strange slowness when using rJava from R that I don't
have if I use the same software outside of R:

1. If we do this it takes over 90 seconds on my Vista PC under R
2.10.0, rJava 0.8-1 and rSymPy 0.1-4

# we don't use rSymPy for anything below except to access the
#     jython.jar in it and the sympy python package in it
# MAKE SURE YOU ARE USING rSymPy 0.1-4 (which just appeared on CRAN)

# set up path to jython.jar
library(rSymPy)
jython.jar<- system.file("jython.jar", package = "rSymPy")
if (.Platform$OS == "windows")
       jython.jar<- gsub("/", "\\", jython.jar, fixed = TRUE)

# load jython and then import sympy
# Importing sympy takes more of the time.
.jinit(jython.jar)
jy<- .jnew("org.python.util.PythonInterpreter")
jy$exec("from sympy import *")


2. But if we do it by hand it takes under 30 seconds:

C:\Users\Gabor\Documents\R>cd win-library/2.10/rSymPy

C:\Users\Gabor\Documents\R\win-library\2.10\rSymPy>java -jar jython.jar
