This is comparing

1. sympy + Jython to
2. sympy + Jython + R/rJava

Its exactly the same software in both cases except its called directly
in one case and via rJava in the other case.  I would have expected
that running the same software takes the same amount of time whether
called directly or via rJava -- not three times as long.

rSymPy is not involved in this comparison at all and library(rSymPy)
is only there to bring in the jar file and sympy since they are
included in the rSymPy distribution but none of rSymPy itself is
involved in this comparison and this was pointed out in the original
email.


