real    0m51.642s
user    0m42.004s
sys     0m2.220s

unpacking, setting the classpath, and the python.path property:

real    0m15.178s
user    0m13.994s
sys     0m0.546s




It does, however not make too much difference for java when invoked directly

[romain@santorini rsp]$ time java -Dpython.path=Lib -cp jython.jar:. 
LoadSymPy

real    0m13.413s
user    0m12.379s
sys     0m0.439s
[romain@santorini rsp]$ time java -Dpython.path=Lib -cp jython:. LoadSymPy

real    0m13.363s
user    0m12.369s
sys     0m0.445s

Here is the LoadSymPy class :

import org.python.util.PythonInterpreter ;

public class LoadSymPy {

         public static void main(String[] args){
                 PythonInterpreter jy = new PythonInterpreter() ;
                 jy.exec( "from sympy import *" ) ;
                 System.exit( 0 ) ;
         }

}

