I've set verbose to true in RJavaClassLoader and run this script:

require( rJava )
.jinit( )
.jaddClassPath("jython.jar" )

# .jinit( parameters = "-Dpython.path=/tmp/rsp/Lib/:."   )

rjcl <- rJava:::.rJava.class.loader
rjcl$verbose <- TRUE

jy <- .jnew( "org.python.util.PythonInterpreter" )
jy$exec( "from sympy import *" )


$ Rscript loadsympy.R > log.txt

The log.txt file is there:
http://addictedtor.free.fr/misc/gabor/log.txt

Looking at it as it runs, it feels that the alternative class lookup is 
the slow part (when URLClassLoader fails). It looks from the log as if, 
if URLClassLoader fails, the alternative also fails. Are there still 
situations where the alternative lookup would suceed when URLClassLoader 
fails ?


