Thanks for the info on the parameters.   I still had to try a number
of variations until I got something to work with an unpacked jython to
get it to completely work but the parameter argument was certainly
key.

The following should work where our starting point is the rSymPy
source distribution since that contains both jython.jar and sympy
itself.  We do not actually make use of rSymPy below -- we are only
using it as a convenient source of the aforementioned two items.

We unzip/detar rSymPy_0.1-4.tar.gz into c:\rSymPy and then change
directory to the \rSympy\inst directory where the jython.jar file and
Lib directory are located. We unzip jython.jar using 7z and note that
sympy is the \rSymPy\inst\Lib\sympy tree.  From the \rSymPy\inst
directory we enter R (so that \rSymPy\inst is the current directory
when in R) and run the indicated lines.  Thus we are using unpacked
jython and sympy. The run time in R here is around 30 sec on my
machine which is about the same as from the java command line so, yes,
it appears that the problem is related to unpacking and that using
unpacked jars offers a workaround for the performance at the expense
of giving up the convenience of single file deployment of the java
software.

