However, I regularly run into problems while trying to load an library. The problematic libraries, always show start-up messages. I try to suppress messages, however, this seems not to be the solution.

eg:
66: rc.voidEval("suppressMessages(library(\"ade4\", warn.conflicts=FALSE))");
67: REXP parseAndEval = rc.parseAndEval("suppressMessages(library(\"adegenet\", warn.conflicts=FALSE))");

org.rosuda.REngine.REngineException: eval failed
        at org.rosuda.REngine.Rserve.RConnection.parseAndEval(RConnection.java:453)
        at org.rosuda.REngine.REngine.parseAndEval(REngine.java:108)
        at nl.wur.plantbreeding.logic.marker.diversity.MarkerClusteringVisualisation.createClusterDiversityVisualisation(MarkerClusteringVisualisation.java:67)

The biggest problem is that this error is not thrown consequently. It work's for a while. Then, suddenly, it does not work for a while. Restarting everything does not help. 

Anybody any idea?

Thanks,
Richard

