On SL (10.6) you have to use 64-bit R since Java is only 64-bit.

So install the Leopard (64-bit) build of R from CRAN, then

install.packages("rJava")

check where it is installed, e.g.:

 > system.file("jri",package="rJava")
[1] "/Library/Frameworks/R.framework/Resources/library/rJava/jri"

And then run the example there:

Fino:~$ cd /Library/Frameworks/R.framework/Resources/library/rJava/jri
Fino:jri$ ./run rtest
Creating Rengine (with arguments)

R version 2.10.0 Patched (2009-11-29 r50609)
[...]
 > R.version
rBusy(1)
                _
platform       x86_64-apple-darwin9.8.0
arch           x86_64
[...]


Cheers,
Simon



